# Witch Enchanter: "destroy target artifact or enchantment AN OPPONENT CONTROLS". The target question offers Bot2's Mox Jet and its Curse of
# Predation (an enchantment, an Aura on Bot1 but controlled by Bot2); Bot1's own Mox Pearl and Bot2's Llanowar Elves (a creature) are
# not candidates (! Target), and the Curse, chosen by Bot1, is destroyed. Everything else stays.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Pearl
Mox Ruby
Mox Jet
Mox Emerald
Witch Enchanter
Plains x14

[Bot2 Deck]
Forest
Mox Emerald
Mox Jet
Mox Ruby
Curse of Predation
Llanowar Elves
Forest x13

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot2.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Curse of Predation.Cast(Bot1)
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Llanowar Elves.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Witch Enchanter.Cast
! Bot1.Target(Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl)
! Bot1.Target(Bot2.Battlefield.Llanowar Elves)
Bot1.Target(Bot2.Battlefield.Curse of Predation)
Bot1.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot2.Graveyard = Curse of Predation
Bot2.Battlefield = Forest; Mox Emerald; Mox Jet; Mox Ruby; Llanowar Elves
Bot1.Battlefield = Mox Pearl; Mox Ruby; Mox Jet; Mox Emerald; Witch Enchanter
